aintenance.md-130-- **R2 input** is one candidate `go.mod` with its `go.sum`, by default the\n.flow/specs/fn-113-gomad-reduce-version-pin-maintenance.md-131-  repository root module. Exit status follows the existing convention: 0 for\n.flow/specs/fn-113-gomad-reduce-version-pin-maintenance.md-132-  no invalidated pin, 1 for at least one, 2 for invalid input, 3 for\n.flow/specs/fn-113-gomad-reduce-version-pin-maintenance.md-133-  infrastructure failure. An unknown pin counts as invalidated.\n.flow/specs/fn-113-gomad-reduce-version-pin-maintenance.md-134-- **R2 side effects.** Module resolution runs outside the target module with a\n.flow/specs/fn-113-gomad-reduce-version-pin-maintenance.md-135-  private module cache, because `go mod download` inside a target module\n.flow/specs/fn-113-gomad-reduce-version-pin-maintenance.md-136-  rewrites its `go.sum`.\n.flow/specs/fn-113-gomad-reduce-version-pin-maintenance.md-137-- **R3 anchors** are the existing exact-occurrence byte anchors. An anchor\n.flow/specs/fn-113-gomad-reduce-version-pin-maintenance.md-138-  that matches zero or more than one time fails. The approval digest covers\n.flow/specs/fn-113-gomad-reduce-version-pin-maintenance.md-139-  the changed upstream source and the proposed new anchors, comes from a dry\n.flow/specs/fn-113-gomad-reduce-version-pin-maintenance.md-140-  run, and is passed back on the command line. The transaction covers the\n.flow/specs/fn-113-gomad-reduce-version-pin-maintenance.md-141-  generated outputs: the full set is staged and verified in a scratch copy,\n.flow/specs/fn-113-gomad-reduce-version-pin-maintenance.md-142-  then published under an exclusive lock after revalidating the checkout, with\n.flow/specs/fn-113-gomad-reduce-version-pin-maintenance.md-143-  a marker that lets the next run complete or roll back an interrupted\n.flow/specs/fn-113-gomad-reduce-version-pin-maintenance.md-144-  publication.\n.flow/specs/fn-113-gomad-reduce-version-pin-maintenance.md-145-- **R3 real adapter** is the first adapted module the root `go.mod` has moved\n.flow/specs/fn-113-gomad-reduce-version-pin-maintenance.md-146-  past when the task starts. If none has moved, the fixture bump stands in and\n.flow/specs/fn-113-gomad-reduce-version-pin-maintenance.md-147-  the criterion says so.\n.flow/specs/fn-113-gomad-reduce-version-pin-maintenance.md-148-- **R4 inputs.** Refresh runs on a checkout where the bump is applied. Each\n.flow/specs/fn-113-gomad-reduce-version-pin-maintenance.md-149-  request is discovered in its own target module through one checked-in\n.flow/specs/fn-113-gomad-reduce-version-pin-maintenance.md-150-  request-to-directory table shared with the Makefile qualification list.\n.flow/specs/fn-113-gomad-reduce-version-pin-maintenance.md-151-- **R4 approval** is per request. A request is done when its stored approval\n.flow/specs/fn-113-gomad-reduce-version-pin-maintenance.md-152-  matches the review digest of freshly discovered evidence, so an approval of\n.flow/specs/fn-113-gomad-reduce-version-pin-maintenance.md-153-  older evidence never counts and partial progress survives a rerun. Variants are removed only on a host that can evaluate their\n.flow/specs/fn-113-gomad-reduce-version-pin-maintenance.md-154-  platform; the others are reported and left.\n.flow/specs/fn-113-gomad-reduce-version-pin-maintenance.md-155-- **R5 manual step** means one command invocation or one hand edit of a\n.flow/specs/fn-113-gomad-reduce-version-pin-maintenance.md-156-  checked-in file.\n.flow/specs/fn-113-gomad-reduce-version-pin-maintenance.md-157-\n.flow/specs/fn-113-gomad-reduce-version-pin-maintenance.md-158-## Open Questions\n.flow/specs/fn-113-gomad-reduce-version-pin-maintenance.md-159-\n.flow/specs/fn-113-gomad-reduce-version-pin-maintenance.md-160-1. fn-109 tasks 10 and 11 change the adapter registry and source-inventory\n.flow/specs/fn-113-gomad-reduce-version-pin-maintenance.md-161-   owner, and fn-105 task 8 adds adapters. Should R3 wait for them, or la