 A fixture with a deliberate host-timed draw\n.flow/specs/fn-112-gomad-determinism-assurance-and-test.md-165-  demonstrates localisation at the injected site. Errors: diagnostics that\n.flow/specs/fn-112-gomad-determinism-assurance-and-test.md-166-  allocate on the Go heap, draw from the seeded stream, or change a workload's\n.flow/specs/fn-112-gomad-determinism-assurance-and-test.md-167-  behavior with diagnostics off fail this criterion.\n.flow/specs/fn-112-gomad-determinism-assurance-and-test.md-168-\n.flow/specs/fn-112-gomad-determinism-assurance-and-test.md-169-- **R5:** The seeded-stream draw-site inventory is complete and classified,\n.flow/specs/fn-112-gomad-determinism-assurance-and-test.md-170-  host-timed sites use the M-local stream, and a diagnostic-mode check fails\n.flow/specs/fn-112-gomad-determinism-assurance-and-test.md-171-  the process on a violation. A negative fixture triggers the check. Errors:\n.flow/specs/fn-112-gomad-determinism-assurance-and-test.md-172-  an unclassified site fails the toolchain tier.\n.flow/specs/fn-112-gomad-determinism-assurance-and-test.md-173-\n.flow/specs/fn-112-gomad-determinism-assurance-and-test.md-174-- **R6:** A scheduled soak gate on each platform reports zero divergences over\n.flow/specs/fn-112-gomad-determinism-assurance-and-test.md-175-  a stated N fresh repetitions per seed under load, and retains both traces\n.flow/specs/fn-112-gomad-determinism-assurance-and-test.md-176-  and the differ output on a divergence. Errors: on linux/amd64 the gate stays\n.flow/specs/fn-112-gomad-determinism-assurance-and-test.md-177-  informational until fn-105 R12 closes D12, and says so in its report.\n.flow/specs/fn-112-gomad-determinism-assurance-and-test.md-178-\n.flow/specs/fn-112-gomad-determinism-assurance-and-test.md-179-- **R7:** Each channel named under conformance fixtures has a seeded fixture\n.flow/specs/fn-112-gomad-determinism-assurance-and-test.md-180-  with a positive control or a contract sentence that places it outside the\n.flow/specs/fn-112-gomad-determinism-assurance-and-test.md-181-  contract. README and SPEC state that closure mode compiles no guards.\n.flow/specs/fn-112-gomad-determinism-assurance-and-test.md-182-\n.flow/specs/fn-112-gomad-determinism-assurance-and-test.md-183-- **R8:** Generated-sequence model conformance tests compare the filesystem\n.flow/specs/fn-112-gomad-determinism-assurance-and-test.md-184-  and loopback TCP models with the host OS on both platforms, with every\n.flow/specs/fn-112-gomad-determinism-assurance-and-test.md-185-  declared difference listed and tested. Errors: an undeclared difference is\n.flow/specs/fn-112-gomad-determinism-assurance-and-test.md-186-  a defect in the model or a new declared difference with a reason.\n.flow/specs/fn-112-gomad-determinism-assurance-and-test.md-187-\n.flow/specs/fn-112-gomad-determinism-assurance-and-test.md-188-- **R9:** End-to-end tests drive `explore` and `replay` through the built CLI,\n.flow/specs/fn-112-gomad-determinism-assurance-and-test.md-189-  and kill a real coordinator mid-campaign, resume it, and compare the result\n.flow/specs/fn-112-gomad-determinism-assurance-and-test.md-190-  with an uninterrupted run of the same plan.\n.flow/specs/fn-112-gomad-determinism-assurance-and-test.md-191-\n.flow/specs/fn-112-gomad-determinism-assurance-and-test.md-192-- **R10:** The change-detector tests named in the assessment are consolidated,\n.flow/specs/fn-112-gomad-determinism-assurance-and-test.md-193-  with a retained mapping from each removed test to its replacement and no\n.flow/specs/fn-112-gomad-determinism-assurance-and-test.md-194-  loss of asserted behavior. Test code lines and test count are reported\n.flow/specs/fn-112-gomad-determinism-assurance-and-test.md-195-  before and after.\n.flow/specs/fn-112-gomad-determinism-assurance-and-test.md-196-\n.flow/specs/fn-112-gomad-determinism-assurance-and-test.md-197-- **R11:** The milestones' quality-assessment section, README, and SPEC are\n.flow/specs/fn-112-gomad-determinism-assurance-and-test.md-198-  updated to the delivered state, including the measured soak bound.\n.flow/specs/fn-112-gomad-determinism-assurance-and-test.md-199-\n.flow/specs/fn-112-gomad-determinism-assurance-and-test.md-200-## Boundaries\n.flow/specs/fn-112-gomad-determinism-assurance-and-test.md-201-\n.flow/specs/fn-112-gomad-determinism-assurance-and-test.md-202-- The D12 fix, the D16 clock correction, patch relocation, and interface\n.flow/specs/fn-112-gomad-determinism-assurance-and-test.md-203-  migrations keep their fn-105, fn-110, and fn-109 owners.\n.flow/specs/fn-112-gomad-determinism-assurance-and-test.md-204-- No feature is removed. Deterministic GC, multi-P scheduling, and rr-style\n.flow/specs/fn-112-gomad-determinism-assurance-and-test.md-205-  machine recording remain research items.\n.flow/specs/fn-112-gomad-determinism-assurance-and-test.md-206-- No capability is widened and no test in `./tests` is rewritten for Gomad.\n.flow/specs/fn-112-gomad-determinism-assurance-and-test.md-207-- Pin-repair tooling, including one-command adapter regeneration, belongs to\n.flow/specs/fn-112-gomad-determinism-assurance-and-test.md-208-  fn-113.\n.flow/specs/fn-112-gomad-determinism-assurance-and-test.md-209-\n.flow/specs/fn-112-gomad-determinism-assurance-and-test.md-210-## Decision Context\n.flow/specs/fn-112-gomad-determinism-assurance-and-test.md-211-\n.flow/specs/fn-112-gomad-determinism-assurance-and-test.md-212-The localiser comes first because D12 and each earlier darwin divergence took\n.flow/specs/fn-112-gomad-determinism-assurance-and-test.md-213-a bisect or a per-event logging campaign to find, and the same search would\n.flow/specs/fn-112-gomad-determinism-assurance-and-test.md-214-repeat for the next channel. A digest per choice point reuses the existing\n.flow/specs/fn-112-gomad-determinism-assurance-and-test.md-215-choice-record path and gives a first-difference ordinal directly.\n.flow/specs/fn-112-gomad-determinism-assurance-and-test.md-216-\n.flow/specs/fn-112-gomad-determinism-assurance-and-test.md-217-A soak with a stated N replaces two-repetition qualification as the source of\n.flow/specs/fn-112-gomad-determinism-assurance-and-test.md-218-the determinism claim because a defect at D12's rate passes most\n.flow/specs/fn-112-gomad-determinism-assurance-and-test.md-219-two-repetition checks, and exact replay forces run-queue and select choices\n.flow/specs/fn-112-gomad-determinism-assurance-and-test.md-220-that would otherwise expose a divergence between fresh runs.\n.flow/specs/fn-112-gomad-determinism-assurance-and-test.md-221-\n.flow/specs/fn-112-gomad-determinism-assurance-and-test.md-222-Suite reshaping is in the same spec because the assessment found the\n.flow/specs/fn-112-gomad-determinism-assurance-and-test.md-223-assurance gaps and the test-mass imbalance together: the layers that are\n.flow/specs/fn-112-gomad-determinism-assurance-and-test.md-224-missing are the ones that test the product claim.\n.flow/specs/fn-112-gomad-determinism-assurance-and-test.md-225-\n.flow/specs/fn-112-gomad-determinism-assurance-and-test.md-226-## Planning decisions (2026-10-01)\n.flow/specs/fn-112-gomad-determinism-assurance-and-test.md-227-\n.flow/specs/fn-112-gomad-determinism-assurance-and-test.md-228-Task breakdown settled the points below. Each is a default the owner can\n.flow/specs/fn-112-gomad-determinism-assurance-and-test.md-229-change before the task that uses it starts.\n.flow/specs/fn-112-gomad-determinism-assurance-and-test.md-230-\n.flow/specs/fn-112-gomad-determinism-assurance-and-test.md-231-- **R1 includes repair.** A failing job is reproduced and fixed on a committed\n.flow/specs/fn-112-gomad-determinism-assurance-and-test.md-232-  tree. A failure whose cause stays unknown is recorded as a finding with its\n.flow/specs/fn-112-gomad-determinism-assurance-and-test.md-233-  log and keeps R1 open.\n.flow/specs/fn-112-gomad-determinism-assurance-and-test.md-234-- **R2 gates.** The `gomad3_toolchain` tests get their own Make target inside\n.flow/specs/fn-112-gomad-determinism-assurance-and-test.md-235-  `test`. `./toolchain` runs once with the patched toolchain and once with\n.flow/specs/fn-112-gomad-determinism-assurance-and-test.md-236-  stock Go, and leaves the host tier.\n.flow/specs/fn-112-gomad-determinism-assurance-and-test.md-237-- **R3 has no task of its own.** Each task re-anchors the findings it uses as\n.flow/specs/fn-112-gomad-determinism-assurance-and-test.md-238-  its first step and records confirmed, changed, or refuted.\n.flow/specs/fn-112-gomad-determinism-assurance-and-test.md-239-- **R4 transport.** The diagnostic trace uses its own inherited descriptor and\n.flow/specs/fn-112-gomad-determinism-assurance-and-test.md-240-  byte bound, separate from the 64 MiB Choice Trace. A `--diagnostics` flag on\n.flow/specs/fn-112-gomad-determinism-assurance-and-test.md-241-  `explore` and `qualify` enables it. The differ is a `gomadtool` subcommand.\n.flow/specs/fn-112-gomad-determinism-assurance-and-test.md-242-- **R4 off-mode comparison.** A runtime edit changes the toolchain build key\n.flow/specs/fn-112-gomad-determinism-assurance-and-test.md-243-  and the choice implementation digest, which are part of evidence. Comparison\n.flow/specs/fn-112-gomad-determinism-assurance-and-test.md-244-  across toolchain builds therefore uses a behavioral projection (output\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
